Critical layout rules:
\begin{itemize}
\item Impedance control: 50~$\Omega$ single-ended, 90--100~$\Omega$ differential.
\item Length matching: DDR byte lanes matched within $\pm 0.1$ mm.
\item PDN decoupling: 0201/01005 capacitors placed directly on BGA escape vias.
\end{itemize}

\section{Verification, Simulation \& Test Strategy}
Before fabrication, simulation prevents costly board spins.

\subsection{Signal Integrity (SI)}
S-parameter extraction models insertion loss ($S_{21}$), return loss ($S_{11}$), and crosstalk
($S_{41}$). Full-wave solvers validate high-speed differential pairs.

\subsection{Power Integrity (PI)}
IR drop analysis ensures voltage deviations remain below 3\% under maximum load.

\subsection{Design for Manufacturing \& Test (DFM/DFT)}
DFM/DFT includes:
\begin{itemize}
\item ICT test points.
\item JTAG boundary scan (IEEE 1149.1/1149.6).
\item IPC-2221/2222 compliance for pad and copper spacing.
\end{itemize}

\section{Production Deliverables}
A complete manufacturing release package includes:

\subsection{Fabrication Package}
Gerber/ODB++ files, NC drill files, blind/buried via definitions, and IPC-6012 Class 2/3 fabrication
drawings.

\subsection{Assembly Package}
Bill of Materials (BOM), Approved Vendor List (AVL), centroid (X-Y) data, and assembly drawings with
stencil outlines.

\subsection{Firmware \& Validation Manual}
Board Support Package (BSP), bring-up sequences, power rail sequencing, and peripheral validation
scripts.

